   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can't big dogs potty indoors?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "They can, but the volume is too much for regular pads. Many homes keep a large pad or artificial-grass box on a balcony as a backup for bad-weather days."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How many potty walks does a large dog need?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Adults are commonly given 3–4 potty chances a day. For high-energy breeds, make one or two of them longer walks."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "My big dog hasn't gone all day. Is that okay?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Weather often makes them hold it, but holding it long is hard on the body. Take a short trip out, and if they strain without anything coming out or haven't peed for over a day, see a vet right away."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is a Jindo a large dog?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Jindos are usually classed as medium-sized. They share the same outdoor-only habit, though, so the care tips here apply as is."
   }
  }
